---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE } from '../utils/site-config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us"
  description="Who we are, how we research our guides, and why we focus on methods that can actually be followed."
>
  <div class="container--narrow">
    <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About Us' }]} />

    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>About {SITE.title}</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="page-body">
      <p>
        {SITE.title} publishes practical guides for everyday household problems —
        cleaning, organizing, small repairs, and cutting household costs. Every guide
        is written to be followed, not skimmed.
      </p>

      <h2>What makes our guides different</h2>
      <p>
        Most household advice online stops at the general idea: "use vinegar," "clean
        the filter," "lower your thermostat." That is not enough to actually do the job.
      </p>
      <p>Our guides are built around three requirements:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Specific quantities and times.</strong> Ratios, temperatures, dwell
          times, and dilution levels — not vague instructions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Explicit limits.</strong> What the method does not work on, which
          surfaces to avoid, and when to call a professional instead.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The mechanism.</strong> A short explanation of <em>why</em> a method
          works, so you can reason about substitutions instead of following steps blindly.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>How we research and write</h2>
      <p>
        Our guides are compiled from product manufacturer instructions, published
        guidance from consumer and safety organizations, and commonly recommended
        household practice. Where a claim depends on a figure or standard, we note the
        source. Where evidence is thin or contested, we say so rather than presenting it
        as settled.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not accept payment in exchange for positive coverage, and we do not publish
        sponsored guides presented as editorial content. Advertising on this site is
        served through third-party networks and is clearly separated from editorial
        content.
      </p>

      <h2>What we are not</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not a substitute for professional advice. We do not provide medical,
        legal, financial, or licensed trade advice. Guides involving plumbing, electrical
        work, or structural repair are limited to routine maintenance that a homeowner can
        reasonably perform; anything beyond that should be handled by a licensed
        professional. See our <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for the
        full scope of what we cover.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections, questions, and feedback are welcome. See our
        <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
